    <briefdescription>
<para>Integral of a one-dimensional function. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given a target accuracy <formula id="203">$ \epsilon $</formula>, the integral of a function <formula id="37">$ f $</formula> between <formula id="47">$ a $</formula> and <formula id="48">$ b $</formula> is calculated by means of the trapezoid formula <formula id="204">\[ \int_{a}^{b} f \mathrm{d}x = \frac{1}{2} f(x_{0}) + f(x_{1}) + f(x_{2}) + \dots + f(x_{N-1}) + \frac{1}{2} f(x_{N}) \]</formula> where <formula id="205">$ x_0 = a $</formula>, <formula id="206">$ x_N = b $</formula>, and <formula id="207">$ x_i = a+i \Delta x $</formula> with <formula id="208">$ \Delta x = (b-a)/N $</formula>. The number <formula id="32">$ N $</formula> of intervals is repeatedly increased until the target accuracy is reached.</para><para><xrefsect id="test_1_test000041"><xreftitle>Tests</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>the correctness of the result is tested by checking it against known good values. </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
